  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rhino &amp; Tiger Conservation Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to increase capacity of the staff of the Forest Department of Assam to carry out effective anti-poaching protection and prevention measures; (2) increase capacity of forest staff to implement professional and safe investigative and enforcement techniques; and (3) increase the number of successful wildlife convictions against poachers and traffickers. This will be done by: (1) consulting with the Assam Forest Department management staff to select modules from the PROTECT and DETECT training programs to ensure maximum relevance for field staff; (2) preparing resource materials for trainees; (3) training 25 to 75 of the junior most patrol staff (Forest Guards) and their immediate supervisors (Foresters and Range Forest Officers) drawn from important rhino and/or tiger sites; (4) preparing a quick reference booklet of enforcement procedures: (5) translating manuals into local languages; (6) preparing a final report for sharing with management of the protected area; and (8) publicizing the completed trainings on the FREELAND website. As planning for this training program proceeds emphasis will be placed on training trainers so the Forest Department will be able to effectively pass on the knowledge provided through the course.</narrative>
  </description>
